NAME
    lean-hedgehog - property-based testing for Lean 4

SYNOPSIS
    import Hedgehog
    open Hedgehog

    def reverseReverse : Property Id := property do
      let xs ← forAll (Gen.list (.linear 0 100) Gen.alpha)
      xs.reverse.reverse === xs

    #eval check reverseReverse "reverse reverse"

DESCRIPTION
    Hedgehog generates test cases for a property and, when one fails,
    shrinks it to a small counterexample.  Shrinking is integrated: a
    generator makes a value together with its shrinks, so there is no
    shrink function to write, and a shrunk value obeys the invariants
    of the generator that made it.

    This is a port of Haskell Hedgehog, not a transliteration.  The
    shrink tree is an ordinary inductive type whose monad laws are
    proved, generators are pure functions of a size and a seed, and a
    report is a value that a pure property computes without IO.  The
    library is written as Lean modules and depends on nothing but Lean.

    A stateful system is tested against a model in one of two ways:

    Hedgehog.StateMachine
        Transitions are one type and one function applies them, as in
        Rust's proptest-state-machine.  Closed: Lean checks every match.

    Hedgehog.Command
        Each command is a type with a Command instance, as in Rust's
        madhouse-rs.  Open: a new command edits no existing code.  A
        scenario runs its commands in order, or in random sequences
        when the environment has MADHOUSE=1.

    A failure looks like this, after shrinking:

      ✗ reverse failed after 3 tests and 4 shrinks.

        forAll [0, 1]
        === failed
          lhs: [1, 0]
          rhs: [0, 1]

        This failure can be reproduced by running:
        > recheck 2 ⟨13986901307939748530, 11216038023333209809⟩ <property>

INSTALLATION
    In lakefile.toml, on Lean 4.35.0 or later:

        [[require]]
        name = "hedgehog"
        git = "https://github.com/hedgehogqa/lean-hedgehog"
        rev = "master"

FILES
    Hedgehog.lean       the library; Hedgehog/ has a module per concept
    HedgehogTest.lean   the tests, run by lake test
    img/                the logo
    USAGE               the guide
    NEWS                the changes in each release
    COPYING             the license

SEE ALSO
    https://github.com/hedgehogqa/haskell-hedgehog, the original.
    https://github.com/proptest-rs/proptest and
    https://github.com/stacks-network/madhouse-rs, the two designs for
    stateful testing.

LICENSE
