AI FULL DISCLOSURE
    This software is developed with strong assistance from AI coding
    agents, with humans leading the ideas and the direction.  We say
    this openly because it shaped how the project was built.  If you
    are not happy with AI-developed code, this software is not for
    you.

    The agents did not bring the ideas.  The author(s) have been
    around property-based testing for a decade, fsharp-hedgehog
    included; "Write you some QuickCheck" is from 2016:

        https://blog.nikosbaxevanis.com/2016/02/08/write-you-some-quickcheck/

    Above all, the design is Jacob Stanley's.  His talk "Gens N' Roses:
    Appetite for Reduction" (YOW! 2017) explains integrated shrinking
    better than any document here, and is the place to start:

        https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LfD0DHqpeVQ

    The acknowledgement below is equally important: this would not
    exist without Haskell Hedgehog, written by hand.

IN MEMORY OF JACOB STANLEY
    This library is a tribute to Jacob Stanley, author and co-founder
    of Hedgehog.

    Jacob's passion for Haskell and his commitment to high-quality,
    reliable software shaped Hedgehog in countless ways.  Integrated
    shrinking, the idea this port is built around, is his: a generator
    carries its own shrinks, so a shrunk value obeys the invariants of
    the generator that made it.

    Jacob passed away unexpectedly on 9 April 2023.  His absence is
    deeply felt, but his impact on Hedgehog, and on those who had the
    privilege to work with him, remains.  lean-hedgehog continues that
    work in Lean, in his memory.
